WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.758
"Darb, run!" Zann yelled. "We'll meet you on the other side of the boulder. Then we can all zap away!"

2
00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:12.929
Darb nodded and darted out of sight. The blue dragons waddled after him.

3
00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:17.325
Zann and the others ran in the opposite direction, with Perda in the lead.

4
00:00:17.326 --> 00:00:21.528
Suddenly she stopped, and Zann almost crashed into her.

5
00:00:21.529 --> 00:00:27.336
He quickly saw why. Arrano was nearby, talking to several adults.

6
00:00:27.337 --> 00:00:31.362
"Arrano!" Zann exclaimed. "Where did you go before?"

7
00:00:31.363 --> 00:00:36.783
Arrano turned to face him. "I had to summon the others before you got yourselves in trouble."

8
00:00:36.784 --> 00:00:45.384
Just then Darb and Zing came around the other side of the boulder, running fast. "They're right behind me!" Darb cried.

9
00:00:45.385 --> 00:00:51.022
"Oh dear." One of the adults bit her lip. "You must have angered them."

10
00:00:51.023 --> 00:00:55.403
"Quick! Get behind us," a man said as Darb reached the group.

11
00:00:55.404 --> 00:01:02.274
Zann grabbed Zing and huddled with his friends behind the Dracians, expecting them to fend off the dragons.

12
00:01:02.275 --> 00:01:08.438
But instead of fighting, the Dracians threw themselves onto their knees in front of the small creatures.

13
00:01:08.439 --> 00:01:11.347
"What are they doing?" Gliss whispered.

14
00:01:11.348 --> 00:01:17.933
Zann shrugged. The Dracians were talking now, but Zann couldn't understand their words.

15
00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:23.474
"Weird," Perda murmured. "It sounds like they're begging or something."

16
00:01:23.475 --> 00:01:28.795
Darb nodded. "And they must be speaking in the dragons' language."

17
00:01:28.796 --> 00:01:32.314
The dragons looked irritated as they listened to the humans.

18
00:01:32.315 --> 00:01:36.603
One dragon spit a small glob of lava near the Dracians.

19
00:01:36.604 --> 00:01:43.278
Finally both dragons turned and waddled away. The Dracians climbed to their feet.

20
00:01:43.279 --> 00:01:48.503
Arrano hurried over to Zann. "Let's go before the dragons change their minds."

21
00:01:48.504 --> 00:01:52.926
The Dracians rushed away, and Zann and his friends followed.

22
00:01:52.927 --> 00:01:57.744
Finally everyone stopped in the shelter of a rock overhang.

23
00:01:57.745 --> 00:02:08.187
"Whew!" one of the adults said. "You kids are lucky the first dragons you encountered were lava leapers instead of something bigger and less reasonable."

24
00:02:08.188 --> 00:02:14.401
Arrano nodded. "Most dragons would have roasted you just for looking directly at them."

25
00:02:14.402 --> 00:02:17.080
"What are you talking about?" Zann said.

26
00:02:17.081 --> 00:02:21.489
"Dragons don't usually attack people without a good reason."

27
00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:25.138
Darb shrugged. "Maybe things are different here."

28
00:02:25.139 --> 00:02:32.340
One of the adults eyed Zing. "Why does this dragon travel with you?" he asked. "Is he training you?"

29
00:02:32.341 --> 00:02:38.020
"Zing? Training us?" Perda chuckled. "He's Zann's pet."

30
00:02:38.021 --> 00:02:44.130
"Pet?" Arrano said the word as if he'd never heard it before. "What's a pet?"

31
00:02:44.131 --> 00:02:52.055
Zann was confused. "Uh, he lives in my house and I feed him and play with him and stuff."

32
00:02:52.056 --> 00:02:57.245
"Oh." Arrano's expression cleared. "You mean you're his servant."

33
00:02:57.246 --> 00:03:01.822
Zann laughed, but quickly realized Arrano wasn't joking.

34
00:03:01.823 --> 00:03:09.488
"Wait," Darb said. "I get it. In this world the dragons are the dominant species, aren't they?"

35
00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:14.686
"Of course." Arrano sounded surprised. "Isn't it that way everywhere?"

36
00:03:14.687 --> 00:03:19.776
"No," Perda said. "In Magica, humans are in charge."

37
00:03:19.777 --> 00:03:29.654
The Dracians looked skeptical. "Humans rule over dragons?" a woman said. "Impossible. Who would serve the dragons?"

38
00:03:29.655 --> 00:03:34.821
Another adult nodded. "And what would the dragons eat?"

39
00:03:34.822 --> 00:03:39.639
Zann gulped. "Do dragons eat people here?"

40
00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:44.926
"Yes, when necessary," Arrano said, "though most prefer other fare."

41
00:03:44.927 --> 00:03:54.586
Zann wasn't sure what to say. It was weird to think about living in a world where people were dragons' servants—and sometimes their dinner.

42
00:03:54.587 --> 00:03:56.668
But he pushed the thought aside.

43
00:03:56.669 --> 00:04:04.161
"We're looking for someone," he said. "Two people, actually. Their names are Wyssa and Morb."

44
00:04:04.162 --> 00:04:09.202
The Dracians exchanged a glance. "They were both here," a man said.

45
00:04:09.203 --> 00:04:12.395
"Wyssa left shortly before you kids arrived."

46
00:04:12.396 --> 00:04:19.533
"Yes," another man said. "She only stayed long enough to determine that Morb had moved on."

47
00:04:19.534 --> 00:04:22.607
"When did Morb leave?" Perda asked.

48
00:04:22.608 --> 00:04:30.154
"About ten days ago," Arrano said. "He was here for almost a week, though nobody knew his purpose."

49
00:04:30.155 --> 00:04:34.300
"Did either of them mention World X?" Zann asked.

50
00:04:34.301 --> 00:04:40.865
"World X?" A woman shrugged. "I don't think so. I've never heard of such a place."

51
00:04:40.866 --> 00:04:43.917
Arrano and the others murmured in agreement.

52
00:04:43.918 --> 00:04:51.049
One of the women cast a nervous glance upward as several large dragons flapped past high overhead.

53
00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:53.923
"You'd better return to the wormhole," she said.

54
00:04:53.924 --> 00:04:56.694
"It won't be long before you're noticed."

55
00:04:56.695 --> 00:05:00.239
"Good idea." Zann glanced at his friends.

56
00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:03.815
"Come on, guys. Let's zap back to the boiling lake."

57
00:05:03.816 --> 00:05:07.900
"Wait!" Arrano looked alarmed. "You shouldn't use magic.

58
00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:10.494
Some of the dragons can sense it.

59
00:05:10.495 --> 00:05:13.901
They might get curious and come to investigate."

60
00:05:13.902 --> 00:05:17.020
All the Dracians were still watching the skies.

61
00:05:17.021 --> 00:05:21.636
Their anxious expressions reminded Zann of the people of Skellia.

62
00:05:21.637 --> 00:05:26.047
He wished he could have helped the Skellians escape their watery world.

63
00:05:26.048 --> 00:05:29.004
Maybe he could help these people now.

64
00:05:29.005 --> 00:05:32.838
"Why don't you guys all come with us?" he blurted out.

65
00:05:32.839 --> 00:05:38.728
"We could take you to another world where you won't be ruled over by dangerous dragons."

66
00:05:38.729 --> 00:05:42.704
To Zann's surprise the Dracians shook their heads.

67
00:05:42.705 --> 00:05:47.729
"Leave Drac?" a woman said. "Oh, we couldn't."

68
00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:51.873
"Thank you," Arrano added. "But Drac is our home.

69
00:05:51.874 --> 00:05:54.549
We wouldn't want to live anywhere else."

70
00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:58.671
The Dracians offered to guide the visitors on foot to the wormhole.

71
00:05:58.672 --> 00:06:02.749
But Zann could tell that they were afraid. And no wonder!

72
00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:08.257
He couldn't imagine how it would feel to know that any passing dragon might eat you.

73
00:06:08.258 --> 00:06:14.333
"Thanks, but we remember how to get back to the lake," Zann said. "Come on, guys."

74
00:06:14.334 --> 00:06:20.442
Zann and his friends said good-bye and then set off through the scorched landscape.

75
00:06:20.443 --> 00:06:23.448
"Are you sure we can't zap to the wormhole?"

76
00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:27.122
Perda complained after a few minutes, mopping her brow.

77
00:06:27.123 --> 00:06:31.826
"We'd better not," Darb said. "You heard what the Dracians said."

78
00:06:31.827 --> 00:06:34.694
The group walked without talking for a while.

79
00:06:34.695 --> 00:06:40.663
Zann frowned when they crested a ridge. A patch of tall trees lay below.

80
00:06:40.664 --> 00:06:45.342
"I don't remember seeing any trees like that before."

81
00:06:45.343 --> 00:06:54.567
Zann's heart sank as he realized what this meant. "We're lost!"

